# ─── Maven build output ───────────────────────
# Never push compiled code to GitHub
target/
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.class

# ─── IDE files ────────────────────────────────
# STS / Eclipse
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.factorypath

# IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml

# VS Code
.vscode/

# Mac
.DS_Store

# ─── Secrets — NEVER push to GitHub! ─────────
# AWS credentials / keys
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets.yml
application-prod.yml
application-local.yml
application-aws.yml

# ─── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ─── Spring Boot ──────────────────────────────
spring-shell.log
```

---

### Why Each Section Matters
```
target/
  └── Maven builds your JAR here
      100MB+ of compiled files
      No need on GitHub ❌

*.pem
  └── Your AWS EC2 key file
      If pushed → anyone can
      SSH into your EC2 🚨

application-prod.yml
  └── Contains real AWS credentials
      DB passwords, API keys
      NEVER push to GitHub 🚨

.settings/ .classpath .project
  └── STS/Eclipse auto-generated
      Different per developer machine
      Causes conflicts on GitHub ❌

*.log
  └── Runtime log files
      Not needed in source code ❌
```

---

### Your `application.yml` is Safe ✅
```
application.yml          ← PUSH this ✅
  └── uses ${ENV_VARS}
  └── no real secrets
  └── placeholders only

application-prod.yml     ← NEVER push ❌
  └── real AWS keys
  └── real passwords
  └── add to .gitignore